  "frozen_rule": "Phase-consistency audit of wrong-FIX labels (analysis only; never a solver input)\nFrozen 2026-10-26 before applying to any full run.\n\nMotivation: CDME Shinjuku TOW 283198-283247 (vehicle stopped) is FIX with a steady\n+0.41 m north offset from the reference. The ambiguity function (AF) of 28-30 DD\ncarrier phases is ~0.0 at the reference and 0.92 at the FIX position, and a +-1 m\ngrid search peaks at the FIX position.\n\nData: dd_truth10 export (10 Hz rover epochs, base aligned like the solver), Trimble.\nDD per (system, obs type), reference = highest elevation, rover LLI 0, el >= 15 deg.\nAF(x) = mean cos(2*pi*(DD_phase - DD_range(x))/lambda), DD_range moved from the\nreference with the rover LOS (linear in dx).\nAFn(x) = max AF over a 3D grid within +-0.10 m (0.02 m step) of x, applied\nsymmetrically to the reference and the solver position.\n\nLabels for every FIX epoch with 3D error > 0.5 m:\n  - n_DD < 10                         -> undetermined (few DD)\n  - AFn(sol) >= 0.8 and AFn(ref) < 0.5 -> reference_inconsistent (phase supports the FIX)\n  - AFn(ref) >= 0.8 and AFn(sol) < 0.5 -> wrong_fix_confirmed (phase supports the reference)\n  - otherwise                          -> undetermined\nControls: FIX epochs with 3D error < 0.10 m; report the share with AFn(ref) >= 0.8 and\nAFn(sol) >= 0.8, and the share that would be labelled reference_inconsistent.\n\nPredictions written before the full run:\n  P1 controls: >= 80% have both AFn >= 0.8.\n  P2 RTKLIB Shinjuku wrong FIX > 3 m (112): at most 5% reference_inconsistent.\n  P3 CDME Shinjuku wrong FIX (242): majority (>50%) reference_inconsistent.\nRaw counts are never replaced; audited counts are reported next to them.\nNo threshold is changed after seeing the full-run output.\n",
  "frozen_rule_sha256": "88c2b015ddb6e408dbb6fb0ed55fc671e14a7e43837fc8d8196e40027e75a12c",
