 "cdmeh": {
  "frozen_rule": "Frozen before the full replay (2026-10-26, after one exploratory Shinjuku Trimble run, disclosed below).\nRecipe under test: CDMEH = CDME + --hold-kalman-update (every flag already exists; no code change, no new threshold).\nBinary: develop 2219d1d (bin/gnss-solve-2219d1d, sha256 prefix 332104cb097646bd). default, CDM, CDME rerun with the same binary.\nMechanism (CDME Shinjuku Trimble debug log): TOW 281649.6-281650.0 are correct subset AR fixes (19/25 pairs, ratio 3.0)\nwhile the float is 0.99 m off with position covariance trace 1.8e-4 m^2. At the 5th consecutive fix the legacy hold\noverwrites the held SD ambiguities (cross-covariances zeroed) but leaves the float position 1 m off. Next epoch the float\nNIS jumps 1 -> 52, LAMBDA fails, and hold fixes 0.63-0.72 m off are accepted for 6.6 s (64 epochs; hold jump 0.65 m < 1 m,\nDoppler distance 0.667 m < 3 m). The Kalman hold conditions position and ambiguities together.\nExploratory run already seen (Shinjuku Trimble only): CDMEH raw wrong >0.5 m 190 (CDME 242); phase audit:\n  wrong_fix_confirmed 3 (CDME 69), reference_inconsistent 149 (CDME 123); episode 281650 gone.\nScoring: as the CDME round (Trimble/PPC exact 1 ms, u-blox 0.2 s grid 5 ms, HK descriptive 2/3 m; gate A 0.11 s matching).\nPhase audit layer: decision_rule_phase_audit.txt (sha 88c2b015...), applied to Trimble Odaiba/Shinjuku and the six PPC runs\nfor every solver; u-blox and HK are not audited (raw only). Audited wrong count = raw wrong minus reference_inconsistent.\nGates (per run):\n A raw: CDMEH vs RTKLIB demo5 multi-GNSS: more FIX AND wrong >0.5/2/3 m each <= RTKLIB.\n A audited (Trimble + PPC): same with audited wrong counts for both solvers.\n C' (effect of H on CDME): wrong >0.5/2/3 m not increased (raw, and audited where available); CDME-correct loss <= 1%;\n   missing and horizontal P95 not increased.\n B (fix_recovery_guard.md vs default): reported; expected to fail as for CDM/CDME.\nPredictions:\n P1 Trimble Odaiba: CDMEH FIX within +-5% of CDME (7467) and raw wrong >0.5 m <= 19.\n P2 PPC nagoya/run3: CDMEH raw wrong >0.5 m < CDME (18).\n P3 Gate A: CDMEH passes raw on >= 9 of 10 runs; Trimble Shinjuku fails raw (190 > 128) and passes audited.\n P4 Gate C': CDME-correct loss <= 1% on every run except possibly u-blox Odaiba.\nDecision: if A (audited where available, raw elsewhere) holds on all 10 runs AND C' holds on every run (audited wrong where\navailable) -> propose CDMEH to the user as the documented opt-in recipe that beats RTKLIB; otherwise record as is.\nNo default change in this round. No retuning after the replay.\n",
